  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting law enforcement within the National Parks Agency (ANPN), Gabon</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to improve the effectiveness of wildlife protection activities within and around Gabons national parks (ANPN) through the active use of information generated from law enforcement monitoring (LEM). The project will: 1) Develop tools to fulfill the needs of ANPN&apos;s law enforcement information management. Information management activities include determining which tools and systems are required to fulfill the information needs of Gabon&apos;s protected area managers in order to ensure the effectiveness of law enforcement, implementation and monitoring; and adapt and set up the IT systems for Gabon&apos;s National Parks Agency and MINEF. 2) Improve strategic patrol planning and effectiveness through the provision of information generated from LEM. Strategic planning and effectiveness activities include improving the speed of data entry and reporting of field observations via the provision of tablet computers for park rangers; strengthening GIS and LEM data management and reporting of law enforcement information; and ensuring effective patrol planning and hosting lessons learned workshops.</narrative>
  </description>
